{
  "version": 1,
  "spec": "Myco v0.9 canonical-bytes serializer (L1/SCHEMA §3.1 + L0/cards/AS_anchor_surface.3 + L1/HARD_RULES F16)",
  "description": "Cross-language test vectors for the canonical-bytes serializer. Every implementation (Rust kernel/shared, Python kernel/governance, TypeScript anchor-client) MUST produce byte-identical output for every input below. Drift = L1/HARD_RULES C18 canonical_bytes_render_drift (CRITICAL).",
  "encoding": {
    "tag_0x00": "Null — no payload",
    "tag_0x01": "Bool — 1 byte (0x00 false / 0x01 true)",
    "tag_0x10": "Int64 — 8 bytes big-endian two's-complement",
    "tag_0x11": "Uint64 — 8 bytes big-endian",
    "tag_0x20": "String — varint length + UTF-8 bytes",
    "tag_0x21": "Bytes — varint length + raw bytes",
    "tag_0x30": "Array — varint count + N items in declared order",
    "tag_0x31": "Map — varint count + N (key, value) pairs sorted by canonical-bytes of key",
    "tag_0x40": "Timestamp — 8 bytes big-endian i64 (unix nanoseconds)",
    "tag_0x41": "Hash — 32 bytes raw",
    "varint": "7 bits per byte; MSB=1 if more bytes follow; MSB=0 on last byte; little-endian byte order",
    "float_note": "There is NO float tag. f64 values are encoded as String(repr(x)) — the CPython repr() of the f64 is the canonical wire form, rendered as a tag-0x20 String. The repr is the SHORTEST decimal that round-trips to the same f64 under round-to-nearest-EVEN; exponential iff the decimal exponent x < -4 OR x >= 16; integer-valued positional gets a trailing '.0'; exponential uses 'e', an always-present sign, and an exponent zero-padded to >=2 digits; -0.0 keeps its sign. The Rust (kernel/shared::float_repr) and TypeScript (operators floatRepr) implementations MUST reproduce CPython repr byte-for-byte; see float_vectors below. Divergence = the float facet of L1/HARD_RULES C18 canonical_bytes_render_drift (CRITICAL)."
  },
  "vectors": [
